From: fedora-opd2413 <noreply@local>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 20:52:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] usb: typec: mux: wcd939x-usbss: keep USB2 D+/D- enabled in
 4-lane DP alt-mode

The WCD939x USBSS crossbar switches the Type-C SBU1/SBU2 (DP AUX /
analog audio) and D+/D- (USB 2.0) lines, not the SuperSpeed lanes.

In wcd939x_usbss_set(), TYPEC_DP_STATE_C and TYPEC_DP_STATE_E (4-lane
DisplayPort without SuperSpeed USB3) only set enable_dp = true and
left enable_usb = false. Because the function clears all switch enable
bits before reprogramming, entering 4-lane DP alt-mode physically
disconnects the USB 2.0 D+/D- switches and drops any downstream USB 2.0
hub / monitor KVM keyboard and mouse with -EPROTO (-71).

Per the USB Type-C DisplayPort Alt Mode specification, USB 2.0 D+/D-
is independent of the SuperSpeed pin assignment and remains active in
all DP pin assignments (C/D/E/F). Keep enable_usb = true for
TYPEC_DP_STATE_C and TYPEC_DP_STATE_E as well.
---
 drivers/usb/typec/mux/wcd939x-usbss.c | 16 ++++++++--------
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 8 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/usb/typec/mux/wcd939x-usbss.c b/drivers/usb/typec/mux/wcd939x-usbss.c
index 65700fc7c..b1a4d2c9e 100644
--- a/drivers/usb/typec/mux/wcd939x-usbss.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/typec/mux/wcd939x-usbss.c
@@ -268,14 +268,14 @@ static int wcd939x_usbss_set(struct wcd939x_usbss *usbss)
 		enable_usb = true;
 	} else if (usbss->svid) {
 		switch (usbss->mode) {
-		/* DP Only */
+		/*
+		 * DP Alt Mode uses SBU for AUX and 2 or 4 SuperSpeed lanes
+		 * for video, leaving USB 2.0 D+/D- independent. Keep D+/D-
+		 * routed to USB in all DP pin assignments (C/D/E/F).
+		 */
 		case TYPEC_DP_STATE_C:
-		case TYPEC_DP_STATE_E:
-			enable_dp = true;
-			break;
-
-		/* DP + USB */
 		case TYPEC_DP_STATE_D:
+		case TYPEC_DP_STATE_E:
 		case TYPEC_DP_STATE_F:
 			enable_usb = true;
 			enable_dp = true;
-- 
